# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .actrc — local GitHub Actions runner config (https://github.com/nektos/act)
#
# Usage:
#   act                         # simulate a push event
#   act push                    # same, explicit
#   act workflow_dispatch       # trigger the manual run
#   act -j build-and-deploy     # run only the build-and-deploy job
#   act --list                  # list all available workflows/jobs
#
# Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3) note:
#   The catthehacker images are multi-arch, but if you hit SWC download errors
#   add: --container-architecture linux/amd64
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Use the medium Ubuntu runner image (~500 MB vs ~18 GB for the full image).
# "act-latest" includes Node, npm, and common CLI tools — sufficient for this project.
-P ubuntu-latest=ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Reuse containers between runs for faster iteration.
--reuse
